            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**On 28 August I mapped this valley from terrain and inference, because that was\nwhat I had. The damage assessments came a week later. This map checks the first\none against them.**\n\nThe flood ran on 26 August. Two days later there was no flood outline, no damage\nsurvey and no casualty geometry. Copernicus had been activated and had published\nnothing. So the first map was built from what did exist: the shape of the ground,\nthe course of the river, and OpenStreetMap.\n\nIt ranked the valley by how steep the riverbed is, counted how many people live\nnear the water, and said plainly that neither was a measure of harm.\n\nCopernicus, UNOSAT and the Humanitarian OpenStreetMap Team have all published\nsince. This map puts what they observed onto the same 210 km of\nchannel, and asks a question usually left alone: **how did the guesses do?**\n\n*Scroll to begin.*\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "What I mapped before I had the data"
        }
      }
    },
    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000001": {
      "name": "What the first map claimed",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 8.6,
        "extent": [
          9256882.117232194,
          3081345.6937492713,
          9711959.114141138,
          3416601.8856210187
        ],
        "transition": {
          "type": "linear",
          "time": 2.0
        },
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
            "visible": true,
            "opacity": 0.4
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
            "visible": true,
