            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Three claims, and the rest of this checks them.**\n\nThe valley falls in three reaches: **42.5**, **24.3** and\n**2.6** m per km of bed gradient. That is what decides whether water\narrives as a wall or as a rise.\n\nNothing on that map was damage. No outline existed yet.\n\n**On the map:** the three reaches, reddest where the bed is steepest\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "What the first map claimed"
        }
      }
    },
    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000002": {
