          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {
            "fig-reflight.png": {
              "image/png": ""
            }
          },
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**The outline the first map refused to draw now exists. Twice, and the two do\nnot agree.**\n\nHOT put the water line at **31.7 km²**, UNOSAT at\n**64.9 km²**. Both careful, different ground.\n\n![The same ground graded twice, two days apart](attachment:fig-reflight.png)\n\nCopernicus graded **3,816** buildings, then re-flew one area\nand found **653** more\ndestroyed.\n\n**On the map:** blue fill is HOT · violet outline is UNOSAT · dots are graded buildings\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "What has been published since"
        }
      }
    },
    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000003": {
      "name": "The flood outline against the three reaches",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
