            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**The other claim did badly, and it failed towards alarm.**\n\nWhat was lost sits a median **108 m** from the\nchannel, against buffers of 500 m, 1 km and 3 km.\n\nAnd it fell upstream: **36.1** destroyed per km in the\ngorge against **3.5** on the open valley, where the\npopulation counts pointed.\n\n**On the map:** small red dots are destroyed · larger dots are schools\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Who lived near the river, and where buildings were lost"
        }
      }
    },
    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000005": {
      "name": "Where the first map was wrong",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 8.8,
        "extent": [
          9286336.847685572,
          3109350.3761708955,
          9682504.38368776,
          3401207.8428533585
        ],
        "transition": {
          "type": "linear",
          "time": 2.0
        },
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
            "visible": true,
            "opacity": 0.4
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
            "visible": true,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
            "visible": true,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**One claim held and the other did not, and the difference is not about care.\nIt is about what each was measuring.**\n\nBed gradient is a property of the valley, and the valley is what the flood ran\nthrough. Measured from terrain tiles two days after the event, it gave a ranking\nthe damage data then agreed with.\n\nPopulation within a kilometre is a property of where people live, which is a\ndifferent question from where a flood does its work. The first map used it\nbecause it was there, labelled it as proximity rather than harm, and it still\npointed the reader downstream while the damage happened upstream.\n\nBoth were honest. Only one was informative. **A careful label does not rescue a\nweak proxy**: a reader who saw 156,970 people on the\nopen valley and 1,239 in the gorge took away the\nwrong end of the river, whatever the caption said.\n\n*Draft. Arjun to rewrite.*\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Where the first map was wrong"
        }
      }
    },
