          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
            "visible": true,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**This is the ground it came off. What happened on it is still unsettled.**\n\nUNOSAT call it a detachment zone following an **ice-rock avalanche**,\n196 ha. Copernicus record a **glacial lake outburst\nflood**. The USGS re-typed it a **landslide**.\n\nThree institutions, three mechanisms, one piece of ground. This map does not\npick one.\n\n**On the map:** the brown outline is the source area\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Three agencies, three words for the cause"
        }
      }
    },
    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000008": {
