            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
            "visible": true,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Four organisations counted destroyed buildings. They got four numbers.**\n\n- **2,813** — Copernicus, over four areas of interest\n- **5,048** affected — UNOSAT, over a much larger analysis extent\n- **1,641** — OpenStreetMap volunteers, in the upper valley project\n- **677** — an AI model, inside a single satellite tile\n\nDifferent ground, different methods, different definitions of destroyed. None of\nthem is the number, and none should be divided by another.\n\nCopernicus also ship the ground they could not assess. For one area that is\n**5.2 km²**, larger than the observed event\ninside it, so the total from there is a floor.\n\nThere is still no casualty geometry here. Nepal's\n[NDRRMA](https://bipadportal.gov.np/) publishes the human toll. This map does\nnot.\n\n*Draft. Arjun to rewrite.*\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Four counts of the same thing"
        }
      }
    },
